{"output":"I’ll read the bug report and implementation, make a focused fix, and run the existing tests without changing the protected files.\n\nThe decoder parses incomplete chunks as full lines and has no closing state. The parser also drops falsy values and treats callback exceptions as JSON errors. I’ll fix both files and use an inline probe for cases the single existing test doesn’t cover.\n\nFixed buffering, line numbering, end-state handling, falsy JSON values, and callback exception propagation. Preserved the synchronous API.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, inline node --input-type=module contract probe, and git diff --check. Reviewed the diff.\n\nOnly src/decoder.js and src/parse.js changed. No dependencies installed or protected files modified.","final_output":"Fixed buffering, line numbering, end-state handling, falsy JSON values, and callback exception propagation. Preserved the synchronous API.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, inline node --input-type=module contract probe, and git diff --check. Reviewed the diff.\n\nOnly src/decoder.js and src/parse.js changed. No dependencies installed or protected files modified.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":9,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"pwd; git status --short; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/stream-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":197,"stdout_bytes":118,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-e40641ba5b894391b83bbefeb3599279.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test && node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport {createDecoder} from './src/decoder.js';\nconst values=[], errors=[];\nconst d=createDecoder(v=>values.push(v),(e,n)=>errors.push([e,n]));\nd.push('{\"a\":');\nassert.deepEqual(values,[]);\nd.push('1}\\r');\nd.push('\\n\\r\\nnull\\nfalse\\n0\\nbad\\n\"last\"');\nd.end(); d.end();\nassert.deepEqual(values,[{a:1},null,false,0,'last']);\nassert.equal(errors.length,1);\nassert.ok(errors[0][0] instanceof SyntaxError);\nassert.equal(errors[0][1],6);\nassert.throws(()=>d.push(''),/closed/);\nconst failure=new Error('callback');\nlet errorCalls=0;\nconst c=createDecoder(()=>{throw failure;},()=>errorCalls++);\nassert.throws(()=>c.push('1\\n'),e=>e===failure);\nc.end();\nassert.equal(errorCalls,0);\nconst f=createDecoder(()=>{throw failure;},()=>errorCalls++);\nf.push('0');\nassert.throws(()=>f.end(),e=>e===failure);\nf.end();\nassert.throws(()=>f.push('1'),/closed/);\nconst e=createDecoder(()=>{},()=>{throw failure;});\nassert.throws(()=>e.push('bad\\n'),x=>x===failure);\ne.end();\nconsole.log('Contract probe passed');\nJS\n git diff --check; git diff --stat; git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/stream-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":320,"stdout_bytes":374,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-319d578a46678316dfd0e99df66acd61.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git diff -- src/decoder.js src/parse.js","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/stream-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":22,"stdout_bytes":1427,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-43785b047a590412ca5683b2b3265578.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":53965,"output_tokens":1202},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":18816,